A shortcut, not Palm's app.

HP's Date & Time app sets webOS's system clock and time zone. Lunacy doesn't own the clock -
Android does, so a copy of that UI here could only pretend. This app is an icon that opens
Android's date and time settings instead (appinfo.json's lunacyAndroidSettings, a Lunacy
extension), and it holds no code of its own. Its id and title are the reference TouchPad's
(webOS CE 3.1.0).

icon.png and icon-256x256.png are Palm's, from com.palm.app.dateandtime on the reference
TouchPad, so the icon looks like the one webOS users know. Copyright Palm, Inc. / Hewlett-
Packard; never released under an open licence; distributed by Lunacy as abandonware, like
Mojo and the Prelude fonts.
